Here's a simple HTML page with a "DVD" text logo that bounces off walls:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <title>DVD Logo Animation</title>
    <style>
        body {
            margin: 0;
            overflow: hidden;
            background-color: #000;
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: center;
            height: 100vh;
        }
        .dvd-logo {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            font-size: 64px;
            color: white;
            text-shadow: 0 0 5px #fff, 0 0 10px #fff;
            position: absolute;
            user-select: none;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="dvd-logo" id="logo">DVD</div>

    <script>
        const logo = document.getElementById('logo');
        let x = 0, y = 0;
        let dx = 2, dy = 1.5;
        const windowWidth = window.innerWidth;
        const windowHeight = window.innerHeight;

        function update() {
            x += dx;
            y += dy;

            // Bounce off walls
            if (x >= windowWidth - 80 || x <= 0) dx *= -1;
            if (y >= windowHeight - 50 || y <= 0) dy *= -1;

            logo.style.left = x + 'px';
            logo.style.top = y + 'px';

            requestAnimationFrame(update);
        }

        update();
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

Features:
- "DVD" text logo that moves diagonally
- Bounces off all screen edges (walls)
- Simple physics with no gravity
- White text with glow effect for visibility against black background

The logo will continuously travel in a straight line, bouncing whenever it hits any wall. You can replace the text with an actual DVD logo image by replacing the HTML and adjusting the dimensions in the JavaScript if needed.
